# Quick Start

Get Nocturne up and running in just a few minutes.

<HostingPicker />

<HostingOnly hosting="managed">

## Step 1: Sign up

Choose a provider from the [managed service](/docs/managed-service) page and
sign up with it. The provider runs Nocturne for you, so there is nothing to
install. It gives you the address of your site. On nocturne.run, for example,
your site is at `yourname.nocturne.run`.

</HostingOnly>

<HostingOnly hosting="self-host">

## Prerequisites

Before you begin, make sure you have:

- A Linux server or VPS with at least 2 GB RAM and 10 GB of free storage
- A domain name. A free name from DuckDNS is sufficient

## Step 1: Deploy

Run the [install script](/docs/installation/install-script) on your server. It
installs Docker, makes the keys and passwords, and starts Nocturne. Replace
`nocturne.example.com` with your domain:

```
curl -fsSL https://github.com/nightscout/nocturne/releases/latest/download/install.sh -o install.sh
sudo BASE_DOMAIN=nocturne.example.com bash install.sh
```

The guide has the DNS records to create first. The other
[installation guides](/docs/installation) are for Portainer, for a free Oracle
Cloud server, and for the same steps by hand with Docker Compose.

</HostingOnly>

## Step 2: Open your instance

<HostingOnly hosting="managed">

Open the address of your site that the provider gave you.

</HostingOnly>

<HostingOnly hosting="self-host">

The bundled proxy obtains a TLS certificate as soon as your DNS points at the
server, so once the containers are running your instance is at:

```
https://your-domain
```

where `your-domain` is the domain you gave the installer.

</HostingOnly>

Sign in and you land on the home screen. It stays empty until a device or an
app starts sending readings:

<Screenshot id="first-run" />

## Step 3: Connect a data source

Saying where your readings come from is part of getting started. Every service
Nocturne can collect readings from, and every phone app that can send readings
to it, is offered as a tile you pick from:

<Screenshot id="connect-data-source" />

The same choices are there later, under **Site settings > Connectors & Apps**.

Pick the one your readings come from, and Nocturne asks for whatever that
service needs to sign in. For Dexcom that is the account you already use with
the Dexcom Share app:

<Screenshot
  id="connector-dexcom-credentials"
  callouts={[
    { anchor: "username", label: "Your Dexcom Share username" },
    { anchor: "password", label: "Your Dexcom Share password" },
  ]}
/>

Then switch the connection on. From that point Nocturne collects your readings
by itself, with nothing left for you to do:

<Screenshot id="connector-dexcom-enable" />

## Next Steps

- Point your CGM app or loop system at your new instance: see [Connecting apps](/docs/connecting-apps)
- Invite followers or create a share link: see [Sharing & privacy](/docs/sharing)
- Set up your first alarm rule
